## Protection from internal network addresses

Two layers, both keyed off **`isReservedIP()`** in `internal/webhook/validate.go`:

### 1. Registration-time validation — `ValidateURL()`

Called when webhooks are created/updated (`server/router/api/v1/user_service_webhooks.go:74`). Rejects `http`/`https` URLs whose hostname resolves to reserved/private ranges:

```56:82:internal/webhook/validate.go
func ValidateURL(rawURL string) error {
	u, err := url.ParseRequestURI(rawURL)
	// ...
	if u.Scheme != "http" && u.Scheme != "https" {
		return status.Errorf(codes.InvalidArgument, "webhook URL must use http or https scheme, got %q", u.Scheme)
	}

	ips, err := net.LookupHost(u.Hostname())
	// ...
	for _, ipStr := range ips {
		ip := net.ParseIP(ipStr)
		if ip != nil && isReservedIP(ip) {
			return status.Errorf(codes.InvalidArgument, "webhook URL must not resolve to a reserved or private IP address")
		}
	}
```

Blocked ranges are defined in **`reservedCIDRs`** (loopback, RFC-1918, link-local/IMDS, IPv6 ULA/link-local):

```14:23:internal/webhook/validate.go
var reservedCIDRs = []string{
	"127.0.0.0/8",    // IPv4 loopback
	"10.0.0.0/8",     // RFC-1918 class A
	"172.16.0.0/12",  // RFC-1918 class B
	"192.168.0.0/16", // RFC-1918 class C
	"169.254.0.0/16", // Link-local / cloud IMDS
	"::1/128",        // IPv6 loopback
	"fc00::/7",       // IPv6 unique local
	"fe80::/10",      // IPv6 link-local
}
```

### 2. Delivery-time dial guard — `safeDialContext()`

`safeClient` uses a custom `Transport.DialContext` that **re-resolves the hostname at connect time** and blocks reserved/private IPs (anti–DNS-rebinding):

